---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import EvidenceImage from '../components/EvidenceImage.astro';
import {site} from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title={"Executive Assistance & Operations Work Samples"} description="Selected work samples in executive scheduling, travel research and project coordination."><section class="section case-hero"><a class="back-link" href="/#operations">← Executive operations</a><p class="eyebrow">Work samples / For recruiters &amp; hiring teams</p><h1>Structure for<br/> the moving parts.</h1><p class="case-intro">A curated view of how I organise time, information and work. The tools change; the aim stays the same: clear priorities and reliable follow-through.</p><p class="privacy-note">Selected samples are cropped or redacted to protect confidential details.</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Work sample categories"><a href="#scheduling">Calendar &amp; scheduling</a><a href="#travel-research">Travel &amp; research</a><a href="#project-management">Project &amp; task management</a></nav></section>
<section id="scheduling" class="section sample-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / Calendar &amp; executive scheduling</p><h2>Make time intentional.</h2></div><p>Time-blocking, availability management, meeting coordination, scheduling buffers and calendar organization.</p></div><EvidenceImage id="calendar" alt="Google Calendar week showing daily meetings, availability windows, lunch and scheduling buffers" caption="Personal scheduling demonstration. Account details are excluded. This illustrates calendar organisation; it is not presented as proof of managing another person’s calendar."/><div class="sample-notes"><p><strong>Time-blocking</strong><br/>Protect focused work, meetings and breaks with a readable weekly structure.</p><p><strong>Availability &amp; buffers</strong><br/>Leave room between commitments and make bookable windows clear.</p><p><strong>Coordination</strong><br/>Use priorities, preparation and follow-up to support an executive schedule.</p></div></section>
<section id="travel-research" class="section sample-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Travel &amp; research</p><h2>Think through<br/> the whole journey.</h2></div><p>Itinerary preparation, destination research, booking coordination, information organization and contingency planning.</p></div><div class="sample-split"><div><EvidenceImage id="travel" alt="Executive Travel Command Center overview with private dates and route details removed" caption="A central travel reference. Private itineraries and family details remain withheld."/><a class="text-link" href="/travel-command-center/">Read the Executive Travel case study ↗</a></div><div><h3>Research that supports decisions.</h3><p>The supplied research collection includes a comparative review of project management tools, travel planning documents and destination research.</p><EvidenceImage id="research" alt="Historical spreadsheet research comparing project management tools and presenting charts" caption="Historical research sample, not current pricing or product advice. Supplied as a vector PDF with no embedded image; rendered for inspection."/><p class="evidence-note-text">Detailed travel documents remain private. The public case study explains the information structure and coordination responsibilities.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="project-management" class="section sample-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / Project &amp; task management</p><h2>Make progress visible.</h2></div><p>Task ownership, project visibility, scheduling, progress tracking, content planning and follow-up coordination.</p></div><EvidenceImage id="monday" alt="Monday.com dashboard showing project stage, active projects, a timeline and status groups; project names and dates obscured" caption="Sanitized dashboard work sample. Project identifiers and dates are obscured; displayed counts describe the sample interface, not a claimed client result."/><div class="sample-split"><div><h3>From tasks to an overview.</h3><p>A useful project view makes stage, timing and status understandable at a glance. Coordination adds the human follow-through: clarify ownership, surface dependencies and check the next action.</p><ul class="plain-list"><li>Monday.com dashboards and task tracking</li><li>Trello coordination and workflow planning</li><li>Airtable content scheduling and structured records</li></ul></div><EvidenceImage id="airtable-content" alt="Sanitized Airtable content schedule with post numbers, dates, weeks and formats" caption="Selected content-planning columns. Account details, editorial themes, captions and private image links are excluded."/></div></section>
<section class="contact-band"><div class="section case-cta"><div><p class="eyebrow">Executive support · Operations · Digital systems</p><h2>Let's talk about<br/> your team.</h2></div><div><a class="button light" href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Executive%20Operations%20role%20and%20CV%20request`}>Request my résumé ↗</a><a class="text-link" href={site.linkedin}>Connect on LinkedIn ↗</a></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
